{#
    Nothing to show, said in the product's voice, with the one thing that would change it.
    `lists/EmptyState`.

    Parameters:
      sentence  what happened, in the product's voice. Fraunces, because this is the product
                speaking about itself rather than the interface labelling a control
      detail    optional, one line of chrome under it. The filtered case says how many are
                hidden, because that number is the argument for clearing the filter
      action    optional, {label, href}: the way out. An empty state with no way out is a dead
                end with good manners
      pattern   optional, a BadgeDesign. The drawn badge is the only illustration this product
                owns: no spot illustrations, no mascot, no empty-box icon. `.empty__mark` dims
                it so it reads as an absence rather than as decoration

    An empty list and an empty filter are different pages. "You have no badges" and "your filter
    matched none of your badges" send the reader to two different places and only one of them is
    the reader's fault; a card picks the sentence, this partial only renders it.
#}
<div class="empty">
    {% if pattern is defined and pattern is not null %}
        <div class="empty__mark">{{ badge(pattern, 120) }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="voice" style="margin:0 auto 8px">{{ sentence }}</p>
    {% if detail is defined and detail is not empty %}
        <p class="body-sm" style="margin:0 0 16px;color:var(--ink-muted)">{{ detail }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if action is defined and action is not null %}
        <a class="btn" href="{{ action.href }}">{{ action.label }}</a>
    {% endif %}
</div>
